SUMMARY:Jeremy Camp with Micah Christopher
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: $39 $59 $69 $79 \nSpend an inspiring evening with Jeremy Camp\, one of contemporary Christian music’s most influential and enduring artists. Known for his powerful blend of worship and rock\, Camp has spent more than two decades creating music that connects deeply with audiences through messages of hope\, perseverance\, and faith. \nWith chart-topping songs like “I Still Believe\,” “Walk by Faith\,” and “There Will Be a Day\,” his live performances are both uplifting and deeply personal—bringing together heartfelt storytelling and dynamic musicianship. \nCamp’s impact on Christian music has earned him widespread recognition\, including multiple GMA Dove Awards—with wins for New Artist of the Year and Male Vocalist of the Year—along with numerous additional nominations across his career. He has also received American Music Award nominations for Favorite Contemporary Inspirational Artist and a Grammy Award nomination for Best Pop/Contemporary Gospel Album. \nBacked by a talented band and delivered with authenticity\, this concert offers an evening of meaningful music and connection. Whether you’ve followed his career for years or are discovering his music for the first time\, Jeremy Camp’s live performance is an experience that leaves a lasting impression. \nNashville-based Christian artist and songwriter Micah Christopher creates music rooted in honest stories\, real life\, and the hope found in Jesus. Originally from Missouri\, Micah spent more than a decade serving in local church ministry before moving to Nashville to pursue music full-time. \nBlending heartfelt lyrics\, rich guitar work\, and a grounded faith\, Micah’s songs—including “Grace Happened\,” “Well Water\,” “White Knuckles\,” and “That’s Who Jesus Is”—meet listeners where they are while pointing toward the transforming power of grace. Experience an uplifting evening of worship\, storytelling\, and authentic Christian music with an artist whose passion is helping people connect more deeply with Jesus. \nFor certain concerts\, audience members may prefer to stand or dance\, especially when encouraged by the artist to do so. Guest expectations differ\, so we simply ask all attendees to extend mutual respect toward one another and maintain awareness of those around them. Our staff will only intervene in matters of safety or when behavior is deemed unruly\, combative\, or disruptive to the overall performance.
URL:https://amtshows.com/show/jeremy-camp-2026/
LOCATION:American Music Theatre\, 2425 Lincoln Hwy East\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17605\, United States
CATEGORIES:Celebrity Concerts
