SUMMARY:ZZ Top: The Big One
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: $99 $119 $139 $159\n \nZZ Top Silver Premium Ticket Package  $309 \nPackage includes \n\n(1) Ticket located in the first 15 rows of the venue\nLimited edition ZZ Top merchandise – exclusive to VIP packages\n\nRock legends ZZ Top have been delivering their signature blend of blues\, boogie\, and hard rock for over half a century. Formed in Houston in 1969 by Billy Gibbons\, Dusty Hill\, and Frank Beard\, the band rose to national prominence with Tres Hombres and the enduring hit “La Grange\,” before reaching global superstardom with 1983’s Eliminator and iconic tracks like “Sharp Dressed Man” and “Legs.” \nFamed for their unmistakable look—long beards\, hot rods\, and spinning guitars—ZZ Top became one of MTV’s defining acts while staying true to their deep blues roots. Their influences span legends like Muddy Waters\, B.B. King\, and Jimi Hendrix\, shaping a sound that is both timeless and instantly recognizable. \nWith millions of records sold\, decades of worldwide touring\, and an induction into the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame by Keith Richards\, ZZ Top remains one of the most enduring forces in rock. Following the passing of Dusty Hill\, longtime guitar tech Elwood Francis stepped in on bass\, helping carry the band’s legacy forward. \nStill going strong\, ZZ Top continues to bring their trademark groove\, grit\, and swagger to audiences everywhere—driven by their enduring mantra: “Tone\, Taste\, and Tenacity.” \nFor certain concerts\, audience members may prefer to stand or dance\, especially when encouraged by the artist to do so. Guest expectations differ\, so we simply ask all attendees to extend mutual respect toward one another and maintain awareness of those around them. Our staff will only intervene in matters of safety or when behavior is deemed unruly\, combative\, or disruptive to the overall performance.
URL:https://amtshows.com/show/zz-top-the-big-one/
